(Source: Simon Willison's Weblog | Published: 2026-11-23T23:40:49+00:00) Tj
T*
(Link: https://simonwillison.net/2026/Nov/23/glm-54/) Tj
T*
(GLM-5.4: Toward Generalized Coding with Our First Loop Transformer GLM 5.4 is now available) Tj
T*
(from Chinese AI lab Z.ai. It's their first model to use a looped transformer architecture,) Tj
T*
(which they describe like this: In a standard Transformer, each layer runs once per forward) Tj
T*
(pass. In a Loop Transformer, a group of weight-shared layers runs for multiple iterations,) Tj
T*
(refining the hidden states from the previous pass. This gives us a deeper network without) Tj
T*
(increasing the parameter count. This is the second mention of looped transformers I've seen in) Tj
T*
(the past week - the first was Inkling 2 Mini from Thinking Machines Lab on November 20th, who) Tj
T*
(said: Inkling 2 Mini is a looped transformer, running the middle layers of the model three) Tj
T*
(times for every token. This allows the model to apply more reasoning and reach the right answer) Tj
T*
(with fewer tokens, especially on tasks such as agentic coding that depend on reasoning quality.) Tj
T*
(GLM 5.4 is not \(yet?\) available as open weights. I tried it out using the Z.ai API, for which I) Tj
T*
(had to sign up for their Coding Plan subscription because 5.4 cannot currently be accessed) Tj
T*
(through the regular API. It turns out both coding plan and regular API share the same...) Tj
